    "stem": [
      {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Amino acids are the monomers that are used to produce proteins in organisms. Amino acids also have other, non-protein, roles in the body.",
        "source": {
          "qp": 19
        }
      }
    ],
    "parts": [
      {
        "key": "a",
        "type": "short",
        "marks": 2,
        "source": {
          "qp": 19,
          "ms": 15
        },
        "stem": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Fig. 7.1 shows the structures of five amino acids with varying numbers and arrangements of carbon atoms.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 19
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "figure",
            "id": "fig7.1",
            "caption": "Fig. 7.1",
            "src": "figures/q7_fig7_1.png",
            "alt": "Displayed molecular structures of asparagine, leucine, methionine, proline and serine.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 19
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "In the liver, one of these amino acids can be converted to pyruvate and one of these amino acids can be converted to oxaloacetate.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 19
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Suggest which of the amino acids shown in Fig. 7.1 would be most directly converted to:",
            "source": {
              "qp": 19
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "list",
            "items": [
              "pyruvate",
              "oxaloacetate."
            ],
            "source": {
              "qp": 19
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "answerLines",
            "labels": [
              "amino acid converted to pyruvate",
              "amino acid converted to oxaloacetate"
            ]
          }
        ],
        "topics": [
          {
            "ref": "14.1(3)",
            "role": "primary"
          },
          {
            "ref": "12.2(2)",
            "role": "secondary"
          },
          {
            "ref": "12.2(5)",
            "role": "secondary"
          }
        ],
        "markScheme": {
          "instruction": null,
          "guidance": [],
          "points": [
            {
              "n": 1,
              "text": "(pyruvate) – serine <b>; </b>",
